{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GgssoKipmKpiuH6n5YN6y4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ICLR 2026 reviewer guide overall rating scale 1-10 soundness presentation contribution definitions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf/fc617925adb22d34e7a2d31f68541c7f3f35ddb6.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2026\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=Fllp8l6Puy\"},{\"title\":\"A Retrospective on the ICLR 2026 Review Process – ICLR Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.iclr.cc/2026/03/31/a-retrospective-on-the-iclr-2026-review-process/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2022 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2022/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Is Peer Review Really in Decline? Analyzing Review Quality across Venues and Time\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.15172\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the ICLR 2026 reviewer guide. Here's what I found:\n\nThe Overall Score is rated on a scale from 1 to 10, where 1 represents the lowest score and 10 the highest, with 5 indicating the paper is borderline for rejection and 6 suggesting it is near acceptance.\n\nThe reviewer guide covers several key evaluation dimensions: Soundness, Presentation, Contribution, and an Overall Score.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the specific definitions for each of these dimensions (Soundness, Presentation, and Contribution) from the ICLR 2026 reviewer guide itself. While I found one search result that references the ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide page, the detailed definitions for each scoring category were not included in the retrieved content. You may want to visit the official ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide directly at https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide to see the complete scoring definitions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17abd94c-441a-4590-97d9-9458f106f7c0","uuid":"39846959-af08-48e1-83ab-58c79d87239f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:01:02.872Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ICLR 2026 reviewer guide overall rating scale 1-10 soundness presentation contribution definitions","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01B551qHHbiPsE8T4NgcfuLw","content":[{"title":"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025","url":"https://openreview.net/pdf/fc617925adb22d34e7a2d31f68541c7f3f35ddb6.pdf"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2026","url":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=Fllp8l6Puy"},{"title":"A Retrospective on the ICLR 2026 Review Process – ICLR Blog","url":"https://blog.iclr.cc/2026/03/31/a-retrospective-on-the-iclr-2026-review-process/"},{"title":"ICLR 2022 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2022/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Is Peer Review Really in Decline? Analyzing Review Quality across Venues and Time","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.15172"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the ICLR 2026 reviewer guide. Here's what I found:\n\nThe Overall Score is rated on a scale from 1 to 10, where 1 represents the lowest score and 10 the highest, with 5 indicating the paper is borderline for rejection and 6 suggesting it is near acceptance.\n\nThe reviewer guide covers several key evaluation dimensions: Soundness, Presentation, Contribution, and an Overall Score.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the specific definitions for each of these dimensions (Soundness, Presentation, and Contribution) from the ICLR 2026 reviewer guide itself. While I found one search result that references the ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide page, the detailed definitions for each scoring category were not included in the retriev