{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019PeTq9qR7ueEtryZssNuW4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on my search, ICLR 2026 uses a rating scale of {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10}. Let me use what I know about ICLR rating scales:\n\nFor ICLR 2026, the scale is {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10}:\n- 10: Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\n- 8: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept  \n- 6: Marginally above acceptance threshold\n\n\n- 4: Marginally below acceptance threshold\n- 2: Strong reject\n- 0: Trivial or wrong\n\nI have what I need to move forward. Now I'll set up the review process with two independent reviewers—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—then have them cross-share findings, discuss convergence, and synthesize final recommendations.\n\nDispatching both reviewers in parallel now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":67237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17abd94c-441a-4590-97d9-9458f106f7c0","uuid":"007da570-27ef-4cd1-ba16-00323fc94eb2"}
